Perform client services and support the State Compliance department on day-to-day duties:
Review questionnaire and business model assessment with client;
Consolidate & compile applications;
Review applications for accuracy and completion;
Review outgoing and incoming physical mail (electronically if working remote);
Manage client communication and ensure their needs are met;
Assist Application Specialist in resolving deficiencies highlighted by the Board on behalf of clients;
Update internal database to reflect application progression;
Administrative work (basic Microsoft Word skills required);
Special projects may be assigned on an as-needed basis.

· Understanding of foundational ITIL policies;
· Use industry best practices and incorporating OTI policies as well as developing and implementing internal / external procedures, policies and strategic changes that are beneficial to the organization;
· Offer training and guidance to facilitate the adoption of said policies and procedures;
· Provide 24x7x365 production support;
· Own the Incident Management processes and procedures and adhere to a metrics driven management style;
· Provide daily/weekly/monthly statistics on all aspects of production support by vendors as well as producing monthly quality reports and reviews for all production support to supporting agencies;
· Ability to understand and interpret customer requirements;
· Manage and / or directly supervise contractors, vendors and appropriately assess their performance to ensure the City aggressively negotiates and receives quality performance and value benchmarked to industry standards;
· Establish and monitor support team compliance with SLA’s and OLA’s;
· Keep an open mind to the adoption of technology, and interpret and embrace to provide state of the art support;
· Drive resolution of Incidents impacting critical systems within the production environment to prevent future negative service impact;
· Ensure the 911 vendor support teams adhere to City guidelines during any outages and / or operationally impacting events;
· Communicate status and severity of impact to Executive Management of OTI, FDNY and NYPD;
· Daily monitoring and troubleshooting of tickets to reduce overall ticket count;
· Review all post-Incident and Problem tickets for root cause determination, risk mitigation, and ensure permanent resolution is put in place;
· Facilitate communications and conference bridge calls between internal /external agency support teams and 3rd party vendors to resolve IT operational Incidents including technical email threads, accurate triage updates, Incident resolution approvals;
· Follow-up on Problem tickets created from priority 1 / priority 2 Incidents to ensure root cause has been identified by the assigned Subject Matter Expert(s) along with a short- and long-term action plan to avoid recurrence of issues identified;
· Oversee day-to-day operational process administration of policies and procedures across all Public Safety operational support teams;
· Manage multiple projects, understanding and providing requirements, migration strategies, creating or updating procedures to support projects and post implementation reviews;
· Serve as senior management backup if and when needed; and
· Handle special projects and initiatives as assigned.
